## Was Xet used?

Xet transfer was enabled (`HF_HUB_DISABLE_XET` unset; asserted in the script) and **was used for `model.bin` only**. Evidence: the hub client logged "Xet Storage is enabled for this repo. Downloading file from Xet Storage.." once and requested a token from `.../xet-read-token/d90ca5fe…`; the HEAD metadata for `model.bin` carries an Xet file hash (`95d706516af777831fff6b2c35837dfb450afca078db361910d44a435b24dc2c`). The other five files have no Xet hash and were fetched by ordinary HTTP resolve, because they are not Xet-backed in the repository. The evidence is the client log (`results/run.log`, where `model.bin` is the only file preceded by the Xet message and the `xet-read-token` request) and metadata; no byte-level transfer trace was taken.

## Caveats

Single download at one revision on one date (2026-10-19); the repository can change later, and the reported revision identifies the snapshot measured.
